<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius Civilis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/69">69</a>–70</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Gaius Julius Civilis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius Civilis was a Batavian noble and Roman auxiliary commander who led the Batavian revolt of 69 to 70 CE during the civil wars of the Year of the Four Emperors. Joined by the Cananefates, Frisii and Treveri, the rebels destroyed several Roman forts on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The Roman general Petillius Cerialis ended the revolt in 70 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-civilis.jpg" alt="Julius Civilis" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brigade Piron · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tervuren_-_%22Claudius_Civilis%22_by_Lodewijk_Van_Geel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
